      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do hardwoods cost more to remove than softwoods?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Hardwoods like oak, hickory, beech and sugar maple take longer to cut and chip than softwoods like pine, willow and poplar. Expect a 10–20% premium on the base price for dense hardwoods — crew time on the saw and chipper wear are the underlying drivers." }
    },
