      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is tree removal covered by homeowners insurance?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Usually only when a tree damages a covered structure — house, garage, certain fence types, or a vehicle in covered scenarios. Insurance does not cover routine removal of healthy or dead trees that haven't damaged anything. Storm work where a tree fell on the house is generally covered, and Roubic provides the documentation insurers need." }
    },
